# routine — leaving from somewhere else is a Go to routine
#
# A routine is an entry point: an area, an hour and what opens there. The walking that got the
# player to an area is not recorded at all; what is recorded is that they ended up there. A session
# that LEAVES the location from an area other than the one it opened in teaches a Go to routine for
# that area (RoutineRecorder.FinalizeAtNarrationEnd) — following a track somewhere and leaving from
# there is a "go there" routine.
#
# So: one move, nothing else, and the visit teaches exactly one routine, of kind goto, for the area
# walked into. Read after LEAVING, because that is when a session's last routine is learned. `inspect`
# answers `routines` with no narration in progress for exactly this reason.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --npc-static --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Test Yard"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# One successful move and nothing else.
strategy succeed
goal move
advance 12 180
click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb move
expect Moved to:

# The filter has done its job and must be dropped before the next phase is generated: it names the
# area we have just walked INTO, and you cannot observe the room you are standing in — so leaving it
# set makes the next phase fall back and fails the run on a narrowing flag that narrowed nothing.
observe none

# Two presses, and the first one is not the exit. A move ends on a node transition, so the footer
# reads CONTINUE: pressing it closes the segment and opens the next phase in the new area, whose
# observation preview then has to be drained before the footer becomes LEAVE.
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90

# The area left from, at the hour it was left at, as a Go to routine — and nothing else.
inspect routines
expect-state routines category=goto location=
expect-state routines Test Yard
expect-state routines time=Dawn
expect-no-state routines category=meet
expect-no-state routines category=gather
quit
